|name2 = Cat and Chocolate
|name3 = Chocolate Cat
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Cat and Chocolate''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Chocolate Cat''' when obtained from [[Chocolate Awakens!]] (may be dropped on the first stage but guaranteed on the second stage) and is level 20 and above.

==Strategy/Usage==
Out of the anti-Dark crowd control units that could be obtained while still in Empire of Cats, Chocolate is one of the most powerful ones due to his Area Attacks with Knockback. He finds the most use in the early Dark enemy spam stages that show up before [[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Bombercat]] is unlocked.

He shines in [[Into the Future]] levels where Dark enemies appear en masse, such as [[Kenya (Into the Future)|Kenya]] and [[Colombia (Into the Future)|Colombia]]. He is a valuable tool for fighting the slow [[Dark Otter]]s in particular, as he can keep those enemies at bay before they hurt any attackers.

Once Chapter 3 of Into the Future is completed, Chocolate's usage falls off drastically because [[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Bombercat]] is then made available.

Additionally, the niche of knocking Dark enemies back is a mixed bag. It can be useful against some enemies, such as Dark Otter or [[Razorback]]. However, it's a generally useless niche in other stages featuring Dark enemies with high knockback counts. Additionally, knockbacks can also be a problem in stages with [[Director Kurosawah]], [[Le'noir]] or other backliners who often punish hard pushers.

{{Job|Classification = Crowd-Controller}}

